    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #311\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed successfully to `bb/relay-114-module-contract-09-12-add-the-e2e-harn-thr_cvs484ubn4`.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements issue #114 ([module-contract 09/12] Add the e2e harness with a cross-module scenario), building on the 01-08 module-contract series already on `develop`.\n\n- Added a third test tier alongside `test:unit`/`test:integration`: `vitest.e2e.config.ts` + `test:e2e` script, using `*.e2e.test.ts` naming and reusing the existing real-Postgres `globalSetup`. The integration config now excludes `*.e2e.test.ts` so tiers never overlap.\n- Added a new `@semprec/e2e` package (`backend/packages/e2e`) with `crossModuleScenario.e2e.test.ts` and two independent fixture modules (`alphaModule.ts`, `betaModule.ts`) loaded through a real `ModuleRegistry`. The scenario exercises genuine cross-module behavior against real Postgres and the real queue:\n  - each module's own structural migration applies exactly once via the shared forward-only runner,\n  - both modules' custom heartbeat rule kinds resolve to distinct, non-colliding schema/nextFireAt implementations,\n  - a task in one module hands off to a task in the other module through the real graphile-worker queue,\n  - one module's declared data migration runs without touching the other module's database,\n  - live `owner_process` drift-checking behaves correctly as a module is deactivated and reactivated.\n- Exported `runModuleDataMigration`/`runModuleDataMigrations` from `@semprec/data`'s public index (needed by the new package, previously only reachable from inside `@semprec/data` itself).\n\nVerified in this run: `test:unit` (83 tests), `test:integration` (364 tests), `test:e2e` (5 tests), `check:boundaries`, and a full workspace `build` all pass.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
