    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #311\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed the fix commit to `bb/relay-114-module-contract-09-12-add-the-e2e-harn-thr_cvs484ubn4` (existing PR #311).\n\n## Summary\n\nAddressed the code-review findings from PR #311's CI run:\n\n- **High**: `alphaModule.ts`'s `handleIngest` and `betaModule.ts`'s `handleRelay` wrote directly to the `items` table via raw SQL, bypassing the choke point. Both now call `createItemWithClient` (newly exported from `@semprec/data`) through the `PoolClient` `helpers.withPgClient` already provides, so property-type validation, idempotency handling, and `onItemEvent` heartbeat triggering apply the same way they would for a real module.\n- **Medium**: the e2e test's deep `@semprec/data/src/testSupport/testDb.js` import is replaced with a formal `./testSupport` subpath export declared in `@semprec/data`'s `package.json`, imported as `@semprec/data/testSupport`.\n- **Low** (non-blocking, resolved as a side effect): the unchecked `rows[0].id` access is gone now that item creation goes through `createItemWithClient`, which returns a typed `ItemRow`.\n- Updated the cross-module queue test to declare the `value`/`sourceItemId` properties on the fixture databases, since the choke point now validates them.\n\nVerified after the fix: `test:unit` (83 tests), `test:integration` (364 tests), `test:e2e` (5 tests), `check:boundaries`, and a full workspace `build` all pass.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
